From eb82cb56f05a5d24ec9bca50f6e9b0d096e37e4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vanetiaho <vangs.vanetia@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:26:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Full-name plane flyover, ambient motion system, jet/otter
 rework, GitHub graph fallback, Spotify vinyl link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Fix hero name hover animation to fly across the entire name width
  instead of just the first letter (percentage transform now resolves
  against a full-width wrapper).
- Rework the 3D hero: sleeker single-aisle jet (tapered nose, swept
  wings, tail fin), otter rescaled and repositioned to read as a small
  rider on a bigger plane, shadows/contact-shadow, warmer three-point
  lighting, and touch-safe OrbitControls (rotate disabled + pan-y touch
  action so mobile scroll isn't captured).
- Add a site-wide AmbientBackground (slow drifting glows + film grain)
  mounted once at the app root, replacing the old flat body gradient.
- Add entrance/scroll-reveal motion to Play, NotFound, and the
  previously-static parts of Projects/Contact.
- Add scroll-linked parallax to the Hero background.
- Make the GitHub contribution graph actually resilient: retry once,
  validate the response shape, then fall back to a themed image-based
  chart, then a plain "view on GitHub" link — never just a dead error.
  No token, nothing added client-side.
- Make the vinyl record a real link to the Spotify track/playlist
  (opens in a new tab) instead of a purely decorative toggle.
- Gate the newly-added continuous motion (Float bob, hover bounce/
  flyover) behind prefers-reduced-motion, consistent with the rest of
  the site.

